        "original_id": "6b4a90bb-dfba-570c-a3a6-63c5eeb40c43",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Giovanni Furno, Vincenzo Bellini, Saverio Mercadante\n- Roles: composer, music teacher, opera composer\n- Places: Capua, Naples, Catania\n\nFacts:\n- Giovanni Furno was born in Capua on January 1, 1748.\n- Vincenzo Bellini was born on November 3, 1801.\n- Giovanni Furno was an Italian composer and a famous music teacher.\n- Vincenzo Bellini and Saverio Mercadante were among Giovanni Furno's students.\n- Vincenzo Bellini was an Italian opera composer known for his long-flowing melodic lines and was called \"the Swan of Catania.\"\n- Vincenzo Bellini died on September 23, 1835.\n- Giovanni Furno died in Naples on June 20, 1837.",
